# Generated assets and model exports
#
# dqn_shopping_agent.zip is deliberately NOT ignored (see below) — it's
# ~425KB, small enough to check in directly, and app.py refuses to run
# without it. A deployed instance (e.g. Streamlit Community Cloud) only
# gets what's in the repo, so the trained model has to be committed for a
# live demo to work out of the box. For a larger model this would be the
# wrong call (use Git LFS or a model registry instead) — noted here so it
# reads as a deliberate choice, not an oversight.
product_listings.csv

